+Keep one authoritative board per event. Editors submit commands over HTTPS; browsers display a revisioned view of the board. Committed changes reach browsers over self-hosted WebSockets: the server operates its own socket connections and pushes each committed revision to connected browsers directly, trading ownership of connection capacity and reconnect handling for low-latency updates with no recurring realtime-vendor fee or provider coupling.
 
